// The raw block is the editing unit of the editor (§4.4, §13.1): editing inside its
// parentheses only examines its phase 1, the block node saves id, the result of parsing is a
// derivative (the edit disables), the instruction is not touched with a call, the update is
// only a block, both clients.
// 
//;
// 
// The cursor in the block is stable: the projection block is the text as written. The draft
// element (author's decision 2026-10-12) is disassembled in its entirety, but the update is
// the narrowest: id node is preserved, only the block has changed.
// program: editor_raw.vish
open_view module
[2] open_view module
run
// expect: output text="16\n" ok=true
// let: blk @{1
[2] pointer 1 @{1 0 7
pointer 1 @{1 0 6
key 1 0
// expect: update view=1 revision=
// expect: node=$blk nodes=⏎  id=$blk kind="n_raw" pieces=["{1 2 30 x}"] note=""⏎текст:
// expect: cursor view=1 node=$blk piece=0 offset=7
// expect: курсор:   print(sum_of() {1 2 30‸ x});
// second client: the same update of one block, its cursor shifted by editing
// expect: другому клиенту:⏎update view=1
// expect: курсор:   print(sum_of() {1 2 30 ‸x});
// expect-not: kind="n_call"
// expect-not: kind="n_hole"
run
// expect: output text="43\n" ok=true
// translation of a line inside the block (with a line indentation) - text as written, the same unit
key 1 Enter
// expect: node=$blk nodes=⏎  id=$blk kind="n_raw" pieces=["{1 2 30\n   x}"] note=""⏎текст:
// expect-not: kind="n_call"
run
// expect: output text="43\n" ok=true
